{"name":"Bedtime Story","hex":"#e1b090","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bedtime story","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A story, e.g. a fairy tale, told or read to somebody, usually a child, before they sleep."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bedtime_story"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bedtime story","blocks":[{"text":"A bedtime story is a traditional form of storytelling, where a story is told to a person, usually a child, at bedtime to prepare them for sleep. The bedtime story has long been considered \"a definite institution in many families\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Bedtime_story_-_Madeline.JPG/330px-Bedtime_story_-_Madeline.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedtime_story","wikidata":"Q464585"},{"title":"Bedtime Story (Madonna song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bedtime Story\" is a song by American singer Madonna from her sixth studio album, Bedtime Stories (1994). In Australia and most European countries, it was released as the third single from the album on February 13, 1995, whereas in the United States, the release date was two months later, on April 13. The song was written by Icelandic singer Björk, and British producers Nellee Hooper and Marius De Vries. Madonna was a fan of Björk's Debut album and, through Hooper, got in contact with her and asked her to collaborate on a song. Not being a big fan of Madonna's work, Björk was initially reluctant at the idea, but eventually accepted. She based the lyrics on ideas and concepts she had always wanted to hear Madonna say, and recorded a demo alongside Hooper. Originally titled \"Let's Get Unconscious\", the demo was re-worked and produced by Madonna and Hooper, who also changed its name to \"Bedtime Story\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/Bedtime_Story_Madonna.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedtime_Story_(Madonna_song)","wikidata":"Q2291771"},{"title":"Bedtime","blocks":[{"text":"Bedtime is a parenting ritual to help children feel more secure and become accustomed to a more rigid schedule of sleep than they might prefer. The ritual of bedtime is aimed at facilitating the transition from wakefulness to sleep. It may involve bedtime stories, children's songs, nursery rhymes, bed-making and getting children to change into nightwear. In some religious households, prayers are said shortly before going to bed. Sleep training may be part of the bedtime ritual for babies and toddlers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Child_Asleep_%28The_Rosebud%29_MET_DT275484.jpg/330px-Child_Asleep_%28The_Rosebud%29_MET_DT275484.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedtime","wikidata":"Q254034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aesop-fables-rare-Book-titlepage.jpg/500px-Aesop-fables-rare-Book-titlepage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aesop-fables-rare-Book-titlepage.jpg/500px-Aesop-fables-rare-Book-titlepage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aesop's fables are short stories, such as The Dog and Its Reflection, that children can understand.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAesop-fables-rare-Book-titlepage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Bjork_Orkestral_Paris_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Bjork_Orkestral_Paris_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Bjork_Orkestral_Paris_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Bjork_Orkestral_Paris_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Icelandic singer Björk (picture), one of the composers of \"Bedtime Story\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABjork_Orkestral_Paris_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Mark_Romanek_Tokyo_Intl_Filmfest_2010.jpg/500px-Mark_Romanek_Tokyo_Intl_Filmfest_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Mark_Romanek_Tokyo_Intl_Filmfest_2010.jpg/500px-Mark_Romanek_Tokyo_Intl_Filmfest_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mark Romanek (picture) directed the music video for \"Bedtime Story\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMark_Romanek_Tokyo_Intl_Filmfest_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/44/Bedtimestory-birth_of_doves.jpg/330px-Bedtimestory-birth_of_doves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/44/Bedtimestory-birth_of_doves.jpg/330px-Bedtimestory-birth_of_doves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot of the \"Bedtime Story\" music video, showing Madonna giving birth to a flock of doves. Authors Santiago Fouz-Hernández and Freya Jarman-Ivens compared this particular scene with Mexican surrealist artist Frida Kahlo's 1932 painting My Birth.[69]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABedtimestory-birth_of_doves.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/MadonnaO2171023_%28116_of_133%29_%2853270953825%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-MadonnaO2171023_%28116_of_133%29_%2853270953825%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/MadonnaO2171023_%28116_of_133%29_%2853270953825%29_%28croppe